MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_001: Heh heh... What a delightful gift.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_002: Such generous souls, to give me this treasured\nbottle of wine after I rescued them.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_003: I will savor it thoroughly when I have some to\nmyself. But, ah! I must get back to the base!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_004: Hey, what are you drinking? Where did you get that?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_005: Hm?! Sha Lan! Well, this is... 
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_006: I've heard that vintage is especially rare. So rare that\nit can't even be bought anywhere.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_007: That is true, but I did not buy it. It was a gift.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_008: I bet it's amazing... I've always wanted to try it.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_009: Ahhh. How can I say no to you?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_010: It's not often that one has the chance to taste such\nan exquisite drink. Pleasure loves company, after all.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_011: Are you sure? I feel like I'm kind of pushing you\ninto sharing.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_012: But I have been meaning to ask... Do you still feel\nsorry for me because I'm from Kunlun?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_013: Well...yes. I would be lying to say otherwise.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_014: My grandfather barely escaped Kunlun with his life.\nHe told me how much he hated it there.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_015: He went on to live in the Hidden Village of Bombae,\nwhere I grew up.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_016: I heard many stories about the severe living\nconditions in Kunlun throughout my childhood.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_017: I have great respect for anyone who survived in that\nplace. I would truly do anything I could for them.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_018: Hm, it sounds to me like he might've been\nembellishing a bit...
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_019: Anyway, how about that wine, huh? I'm excited to\ntry it!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_C_020: Ha ha! Yes, yes. Enough chatter. Let's crack\nopen this bottle already.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_001: I always enjoy your company, Sha Lan. Though the\nmugs do pile up more than usual when you're here...
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_002: Heh! I never say no to more mugs!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_003: Although, it seems like you partake fairly frequently.\nFor a former priest, you're pretty relaxed.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_004: Ha ha! You speak the truth. My name even means\n"he who bends through the world."
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_005: Is your name from the ancient tongue? I should have\nexpected it, since you're connected to Kunlun too.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_006: Indeed, indeed. Your name comes from the ancient\ntongue as well, am I correct?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_007: It does. My name means "the rose that blooms in the\ndesert."
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_008: I know it comes from tradition, but I hardly have a\nchance to mention it. Maybe it'll fade into obscurity.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_009: Impermanence is the one constant in this world.\nA sad and vexing truth.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_010: Hang on, I have an idea. Can you hand me\nsomething to write on?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_011: Uh, sure. What do you plan to do with it?
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_012: I'm going to write out the characters on this bottle.\nI'll make it look fancy.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_013: I see! What looks at first like an intricate design will\nbe recognized by some as the ancient tongue!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_014: It's neat looking, hm? I wonder if we can use it\nsomehow.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_015: Ha ha! I've had the most brilliant thought! We should\nbottle our own wine!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_016: We will draw this pattern on the bottles and sell\nthem. And so the ancient ways will continue on!
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_017: I like that idea! And it just looks like symbols at a\nglance, so the temples probably won't notice.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_018: Plus, I love that it would be on wine bottles. That's\nvery fitting for you and me.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_019: Indeed! What luck that we both secretly inherited\nour names.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_020: Though I am a bit surprised you liked the idea.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_021: I heard the ancient kingdom of Solomon was\nvery particular about passing down its knowledge.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_022: I expected you might say something along the lines\nof, "One must adhere to the proper methods."
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_023: Yeah, that does sound like something I would've\nsaid at some point.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_024: But after hearing your story of the Hidden Village of\nBombae, I started to feel differently.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_025: The people who left Kunlun still pass down\nknowledge in their own way.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_026: Much like how you know your name and its meaning\nin the ancient tongue.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_027: It's the same with this wine bottle. We should keep\nseeking new ways—ways not bound by Solomon's.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_028: So you do not condemn those who left Kunlun as\ntraitors... In fact, you accept them.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_029: Here I intended to help you, but you are the one\nwho is supporting me. 
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_030: I have been a fool. I would like to thank you,\non behalf of my grandfather.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_031: Thank you for acknowledging all that was passed\ndown at the Hidden Village of Bombae.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_032: Hehe. I'm glad. And to show me how grateful you\nare, I'll take a bottle of your finest.
MID_SE_Sar_Yan_B_033: I would expect nothing less. You won't\nbe disappointed!